# Project Bible - Adult Waifu Card Battler (Working Title)

Last updated: January 26, 2026  [Note: Bump this date when you save revisions]

## 1. Game Overview
- Genre: Adult turn-based card battler where players collect waifu cards and fight AI opponents in a story-driven campaign featuring mature themes like violence and political assassinations.
- Engine: Godot 4.6 (locked)
- Platforms: PC (Windows/Linux/Mac) priority, Mobile (Android/iOS) low priority due to TOS concerns
- Art Style: Pixel sprites for characters and effects, hand-drawn cards and maps, Dialogic for story with hand-drawn backgrounds
- Core Loop: In Meta Hub select Hero/Starter Deck, equip Meta Relics/Gear, choose up to 3 waifu companions (affection-based starting bonuses) → enter instanced roguelike dungeon run (finite map, nodes, themed to current campaign chapter) → navigate map → battles (Cascade chaining) → run rewards (run-only cards/relics/gold) → run win advances story (Dialogic scene, affection boosts, unlocks) or loss allows retry (limited per chapter) → repeat until chapter clear → campaign progression toward demon invasion.
- Win Condition (per battle): Reduce enemy HP to 0 before yours hits 0
- Campaign Goal: The entire story builds toward a massive demon invasion. Player choices, allies, waifu relationships, faction standings, and story decisions determine multiple endings — e.g. "You saved the world but X waifu died", "You became the new ruler at a terrible cost", or the true bad ending where the world is swallowed by the demon invasion.
- Single-player only
- Story & Choices: Multiple player choices that alter the story (branching paths via Dialogic)
- Maps & Dungeons: **Finite, instanced roguelike maps per run** (25–35 nodes, procedurally flavored, varying lengths to complete and rewards as the player progresses through campaign chapters)
- Factions: Multiple factions vying for power that the player can help or hinder (impacts story, loot, waifu availability, endings)
- Deck Rule: **Decks reset every run** — start with Hero-specific starter deck (8–12 cards); acquire run-only cards during the run (exhaust/remove post-run); no persistent deck growth across runs or campaign. Permanent player growth via meta relics/gear, waifu affection levels (persistent, provide scaling run bonuses), and story progression (unlocks, faction rep).

